{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "02XG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{S} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0007": "$2$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{S} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-2-product-categories-over-C}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-2-fibre-product-categories}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{example-2-fibre-product-categories}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-2-product-categories-over-C}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-different-2-fibre-products}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{example}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2de0442900e3f6733977e7adc284dbaddb89df657430100dd3ee32acb6c1ca5b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53b0b392afb02dc22c9f8b9d070aba3346a3de2341c5da040433e20c119f787c", "source_text": "The constructions of <MATH_0001>-fibre products of categories over categories given in\nLemma <REF_0001> and of categories in\nLemma <REF_0002>\n(as in Example <REF_0003>)\nproduce non-equivalent outputs in general.\nNamely, let <MATH_0002> be the groupoid category with one object and two\narrows, and let <MATH_0003> be the discrete category with one object.\nTaking the <MATH_0004>-fibre product <MATH_0005>\nas categories yields the discrete category with two objects. However, if\nwe view all of these as categories over <MATH_0006>, the\n<MATH_0007>-fiber product <MATH_0008>\nas categories over <MATH_0009> is the discrete category with one object.\nThe difference is that (in the notation of\nLemma <REF_0004>), we were allowed to choose\nany comparison isomorphism <MATH_0010> in the first situation, but could only\nchoose the identity arrow in the second situation.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ff20cc58d9efa49c565e0ad11fd15ac5a3bda49a7a720f05ea8335eb490cbd9c", "unit_id": "tag:02XG:example"}
